Using the exact canonical default ID did not resolve the endpoint mismatch, while the provider/archive checks passed. This rules out source-input drift and points to evaluation dependence on the batch surface used by the original exact-source build (default plus all singleton configurations). Re-running those singletons is explicitly forbidden, so I’m inspecting the dense evaluator for cross-configuration batching and whether the stored singleton profiles can safely populate the cache without a physics call.
