The dense implementation chunks and occupancy-sorts the catalogue before batched matrix solves, so a default’s binary result can depend on the batch surface even at one thread. A valid construction is still available without re-running singletons: compute every stored `d_i` from its original authenticated default+singleton batch, compute each new `ΔF(A)` from the fresh default+joint batch, then form `Ψ_A = ΔF(A) − Σd_i` directly. Each difference is internally `evaluate_many`/boundary-0 consistent, and the C1 term remains exactly the one already stored. I’m encoding those exact fractions into the reader’s declared `CoalitionRow` schema and recording the cross-batch default gap explicitly.
